# Frontend build-time config.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is inlined into the Next.js build output at
# `next build` time (NOT read at container runtime) — see
# src/lib/config.ts and tasks/devops/OPS-1.3.md.
#
# - Host dev / browser-consumed calls (`npm run dev` outside Docker, or the
#   default for the docker-compose stack, since NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined
#   into the browser bundle too and the browser runs on the host talking to
#   the backend's host-published port):
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# - Only if/when server-side code (SSR / route handlers, running inside the
#   frontend container) needs to call the backend directly by container
#   name inside the compose network (FE-1.2's concern, not decided here):
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://backend:8080
#
# The repo root .env.example / .env is the source of truth for the compose
# stack (passed to frontend/Dockerfile as a Docker build ARG via
# docker-compose.yml's `frontend.build.args`); this file documents the same
# variable for standalone frontend development (`cd frontend && npm run
# dev` / `npm run build`) outside of Docker.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
